  "term": "beta-glucuronidase deficiency",
  "definition": "Beta-glucuronidase deficiency, also called Sly syndrome, is a rare inherited lysosomal storage disease caused by too little of the beta-glucuronidase enzyme. In cognition-related contexts, it may involve intellectual impairment along with physical features such as an enlarged liver and spleen, skeletal abnormalities, and a large head.",
